The plugin targets the public OPUS 2 plugin SDK by LizardMan245:
https://github.com/LizardMan245/opus
Pinned SDK commit: 43b18c97ca0cde430b7d176ca4388fd5d1efeb7d
The SDK/toolchain are external dependencies, not bundled here.
Minimal test-only API declarations in tests/sdk-stubs are based on that public SDK.
No Teenage Engineering firmware/core image is included.

The bounded LZSS4 codec is the project's custom format, not LZ4.
All test framebuffers and generated wire captures are synthetic.
The GNU toolchain build helper downloads separately licensed GNU components;
their original notices/licenses remain in those external source trees.

This standalone export retains production source and plugin artifact bytes from
the development workspace at e2e07295011a2d3d7a0d84b4500f41e082d6f69e.
That hash identifies the original local development history, not a required commit
in this new standalone repository. The original workspace is preserved separately.
